  {
   "section": "answers",
   "items": [
    {
     "role": "eyebrow",
     "order": 0,
     "text": "Straight answers"
    },
    {
     "role": "heading",
     "order": 1,
     "text": "The questions people actually call about."
    },
    {
     "role": "body",
     "order": 2,
     "text": "Our answer library is written from real member service calls, updated monthly, and specific enough that you don't have to phone us to confirm it. Signed-in members see answers matched to their own plan and claims."
    },
    {
     "role": "cta",
     "order": 3,
     "text": "Browse all answers",
     "href": "#"
    },
    {
     "role": "heading",
     "order": 4,
     "text": "How do I confirm a provider is in network before I book?"
    },
    {
     "role": "body",
     "order": 5,
     "text": "Check the directory listing's \"verified on\" date, or ask us for a written verification with a reference number — it takes one call and holds if the directory was wrong."
    },
    {
     "role": "heading",
     "order": 6,
     "text": "Why can the same procedure cost three different amounts?"
    },
    {
     "role": "body",
     "order": 7,
     "text": "Facility fees. A hospital outpatient department, an ambulatory surgery center, and an office bill the same procedure at different contracted rates. Our estimator shows all three."
    },
    {
     "role": "heading",
     "order": 8,
     "text": "What are your prior authorization criteria — the actual documents?"
    },
    {
     "role": "body",
     "order": 9,
     "text": "All 412 active medical policies are in the public policy library, each with a policy number, effective date, and revision history. Your provider can cite them when submitting."
    },
    {
     "role": "heading",
     "order": 10,
     "text": "Where does my deductible actually stand?"
    },
    {
     "role": "body",
     "order": 11,
     "text": "Your accumulator updates as claims finalize, with a claim-by-claim breakdown you can export. If your math and ours disagree, we'll reconcile it line by line."
    }
   ],
